If you have opened the Claude download page lately and wondered whether you need Claude Code, Claude Cowork, Claude Desktop or something called Claude Duet, you are not alone. Anthropic now ships several surfaces that all sit on the same Claude account, and the names overlap: Claude Code is also a tab inside the Claude Desktop app, Cowork is a mode (and now, by Anthropic's own description, "part of Claude") that you reach from the same app, and the Agent SDK is Claude Code packaged as a library. This guide separates the products, says who each one is for, and shows what each can load: skills, plugins, MCP connectors, hooks and subagents.

Short version, as of November 27, 2026: Claude Desktop is the app (free to download), Claude Code is the coding agent (paid plans, terminal, IDE, desktop Code tab, web), Claude Cowork is the same agentic approach pointed at documents, spreadsheets, research and other knowledge work (paid plans), Claude Duet is a separate proactive-agent app in research preview, and the Agent SDK and Managed Agents are the developer routes for building your own agents. Each is priced through your Claude plan or your API key, and every price below is dated.

{% youtube id="UAmKyyZ-b9E" title="Introducing Cowork: Claude Code for the rest of your work" /%}

*Official Anthropic video introducing Cowork. We verified the video id and title through YouTube oEmbed (channel: Anthropic). We did not independently verify every claim made in the video, and Cowork has changed since its January launch, so treat the later sections of this post as the current picture.*

## Short answer and quick picks

- **Best for software engineers: Claude Code.** It reads your repository, edits files, runs commands and talks to your dev tools, from the terminal, VS Code, JetBrains, the desktop app's Code tab, Slack and the web.
- **Best for non-coding knowledge work: Claude Cowork.** Reports, decks, spreadsheet reconciliation, contract review and research, run as tasks you hand off, with scheduled and unattended runs.
- **Best free way in: Claude Desktop.** The app is available on every plan including Free. Chat, skills and connectors are in Free; Claude Code and Cowork need a paid plan.
- **Best proactive assistant: Claude Duet,** if you are in a supported country on a paid plan and are comfortable with a research preview that messages you first.
- **Best for building your own agent: the Claude Agent SDK** if you want to run the agent loop in your own process, **Managed Agents** if you want Anthropic to host the loop and sandbox (beta).
- **Best for skills and plugins authors:** Claude Code, because skills, plugins, hooks and subagents all run there, and skills you write follow the open Agent Skills format.

{% callout type="info" %}
The most common mix-up: "Claude Desktop" is an app that contains chat, Cowork and the Claude Code tab. Anthropic's desktop docs say it plainly: "In the Claude Desktop app, Claude Code is the Code tab. The app also has chat and Cowork." So claude code vs claude desktop is not an either/or. The real choice is which tab, which environment (local, cloud or SSH), and which plan.
{% /callout %}

{% figure src="https://assets.claude.com/1eec21fd9f2fe2cdc0afbb00e826d0bdccac7895.jpg?w=1200&h=630&fit=crop" alt="Claude download page social image showing the Claude desktop and mobile apps" caption="The Claude download page presents one app for chat, hand-off tasks and code. Source: Anthropic (claude.com/download)" /%}

