## How we evaluated this

We read primary sources: Anthropic's pricing page, product pages for Cowork, Claude Code and Duet, the download page, the Claude Code docs (overview, desktop, skills, Agent SDK), the Managed Agents overview on the platform docs, and Help Center articles on Cowork, chat-and-Cowork unification, plugins, skills and Duet's promotional credit. We also read Anthropic's X posts, checking each embedded post through the X syndication endpoint and each YouTube video through oEmbed. Where a claim came from a third party (a CNBC article on Duet, a digest of Anthropic's LinkedIn posts, a third-party index of ClaudeDevs posts), we say so in the text.

What we did not do: we did not install Claude Code, run Cowork tasks, test Duet (we are not on its waitlist) or measure usage limits. We ran HTTP checks on every link and on every media URL. No benchmark or leaderboard compares these surfaces to each other, because they are access routes to the same underlying models rather than rival engines, so we did not invent one. Anthropic's pages change quickly (the Cowork and chat merge was still rolling out as we wrote), so check the dated sources below before buying.

## FAQ

### What is the difference between Claude Code, Claude Cowork and Claude Desktop?

Claude Code is a coding agent that works in a repository from the terminal, IDEs, the desktop app and the web. Claude Cowork applies the same agentic approach to documents, spreadsheets, research and other knowledge work. Claude Desktop is the app that hosts chat, Cowork and a Code tab. Per Anthropic's desktop docs, "In the Claude Desktop app, Claude Code is the Code tab. The app also has chat and Cowork."

### Is Claude Cowork the same as Claude Code?

They share the idea (an agent that plans, uses tools and works for a while) but not the audience or interface. Anthropic launched Cowork as "Claude Code for the rest of your work." Cowork does not edit code in a repository the way Claude Code does, and Claude Code does not offer Cowork's document-focused workflow.

### Do I need Claude Desktop to use Claude Code?

No. Claude Code installs in a terminal, VS Code and JetBrains, and runs on the web. The desktop app adds a graphical Code tab with parallel sessions and visual diffs, but you can skip it.

### Do I need Claude Desktop to use Cowork?

Mostly yes for local work. Cowork is available on web and mobile for paid plans, but tasks that need local files, the built-in browser or computer use work through the desktop app, which must be open and connected, per Anthropic's help center.

### How much does Claude Cowork cost?

There is no separate Cowork price in what we fetched. It is included in Pro ($17 per month billed annually or $20 monthly), Max ($100), Ultra ($200), Team and Enterprise. Team standard seats are $20 per seat annually or $25 monthly, and premium seats are $100 annually or $125 monthly. Prices checked November 27, 2026.

### Is Claude Code free?

No. The pricing page lists Claude Code as not included on the Free plan. The cheapest route is Pro. You can also use some Claude Code surfaces with an Anthropic Console account or third-party providers, per the overview docs, which say most surfaces need a subscription or Console account and the CLI, VS Code and JetBrains also support third-party providers.

### Is Claude Desktop free?

The app is free to download and every plan type can use it, according to Anthropic's download FAQ. Some features, including Claude Code and Cowork, need a paid plan.

### Does Cowork run locally or in the cloud?

Since October 6, 2026, new Cowork tasks on Pro, Max and Ultra run in the cloud, and the "Only on your computer" option was removed. Tasks started earlier on your computer stay local until finished. Local folders are reached through the desktop app. A third-party digest of Anthropic's LinkedIn posts (satori.ml) also describes Cowork running commands in a local isolated virtual machine, so check your own account's behavior.

### Can Cowork and Claude Code use the same skills and plugins?

Yes. Anthropic says plugins added in claude.ai or the desktop app are saved to your account and available in chat, Cowork and Claude Code, and the skills and commands in a plugin work in all three. Hooks and sub-agents run only in Cowork and Claude Code. Plugins installed from the Claude Code command line stay on that machine.

### What is Claude Duet and how is it different from Cowork?

Duet is a separate proactive agent app in research preview, announced October 21, 2026. It briefs you on what needs attention and works when you are away, and it reuses your Claude memory, skills and connected apps. Cowork waits for you to hand it a task. Duet is listed for Pro, Max and Ultra in the US, India, Indonesia, Brazil and Japan.

### What are the Agent SDK and Managed Agents for?

They are for building your own agents. The Agent SDK is Claude Code as a Python or TypeScript library, run in your process. Managed Agents is a hosted harness where Anthropic runs the agent loop in a cloud or self-hosted sandbox. Managed Agents is in beta.

### Is there a Claude Cowork for Windows or Linux?

Windows: Anthropic announced Cowork on Windows on February 10, 2026 with "full feature parity with MacOS." Linux: Anthropic's help center lists Claude Desktop for Linux (beta) as available on all paid plans.

### Which should a beginner pick?

Start with the free desktop app or claude.ai. When you need more, take Pro. If your work is documents, use Cowork; if it is code, use Claude Code. Both are included in Pro.

### Where do I find skills for these tools?

Anthropic's built-in directory is under Customize in the app, and Anthropic's open-source skills repository is on [GitHub](https://github.com/anthropics/skills). The agentskills.codes catalog lists many community skills, such as the ones above.

